Summary of behavioural changes to existing code:

  * Float32 prior distributions are widened to float64 rather than rejected.
  * A warning is emitted when media history is too short for the adstock
    window, which otherwise zero-pads silently.
  * Non-finite variables are excluded from the VIF check rather than aborting
    it.
  * Several input-validation errors now name the offending column, coordinate
    or value.
  * Test-only fixes for protobuf >= 6 and for Python 3.11 mock behaviour.
  * The generated HTML report shows credible intervals on the response-curve
    chart, which previously passed `include_ci=False`, and carries a caveat
    stating that those intervals are conditional on the assumed saturation
    shape.
  * Multi-channel charts use an explicit colour-blind-safe categorical range
    instead of falling back to Vega-Lite's default scheme.
  * The budget-allocation chart is a labelled bar rather than a pie whose
    values were reachable only on hover.
  * Reports embed pinned, integrity-checked chart libraries, icons and an icon
    font with their licenses. Standard generated reports render offline.
  * Mobile report charts use keyboard-accessible scroll regions rather than
    clipping wide charts inside narrow cards.
  * Report text values are HTML-escaped, while explicitly rendered fragments
    preserve chart, table and finding markup. Chart JSON uses script-safe
    serialization, and chart lookup handles quoted identifiers.
  * Geographic allocation diagnostics consider paid channels only. Sampling
    diagnostics preserve non-finite failure signals, and fixed-truth recovery
    ranks are explicitly distinguished from simulation-based calibration.
  * Setup handles custom environment paths; Docker permits non-root output
    writes; CI includes Scenario Planner and a real fit-to-report smoke test.
  * Version checks support a repository's first release without existing tags.
  * Strict sampling assessments distinguish rank-normalized R-hat, bulk/tail
    ESS, divergences, missing signals and metadata-confirmed deterministic
    parameters. Passing those checks does not establish causal validity.
  * Ordinary sampler-option mappings are normalized before JAX's static JIT
    boundary. Local and CI suites use the same bounded-memory test phases.
  * The frozen setup uses a dependency lock; schema source dependencies and
    GitHub Actions use full commit pins.

